# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# raw design uploads — source PNGs already preserved in main's history from
# the original GitHub upload; only the processed /public assets ship here.
/design/raw-uploads/

# KN-138: screenshots pasted into the repo root. 17 of them (39.4MB) were
# committed at top level, referenced by nothing in src/ or docs/, and every
# checkout paid for them. They now live in design/raw-uploads/founder-
# screenshots/ above, which is already ignored — so they stay on disk for
# whoever needs them and stop riding along in the tree. This rule stops the
# next batch landing at the root in the first place; anything genuinely
# needed by the product belongs in public/ under a real name.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Verification screenshots, by the same reasoning as KN-138 above. Agents
# working on this branch photograph what they changed — back navigation, the
# loading and empty states, the capped lists — at a phone width and a desktop
# width, which is the practice that caught a back four drawn as three-and-one,
# a label reading "Shots on target attempted", and a skeleton 8.5px taller than
# the page replacing it. That practice is worth keeping and the output is not:
# 31 files, 6.7MB, referenced by nothing in src/, and regenerable by re-running
# the harness that produced them.
#
# They stay on disk for whoever is mid-review, exactly like the founder
# screenshots above, and stop every future checkout paying for them. A picture
# that genuinely documents a decision belongs in docs/ next to the words that
# explain it, under a real name.
/design/screenshots/

# Claude Code session state and background-agent worktrees — never repo content.
/.claude/
